From 03c012f471ead48f710d2b2af130db9137783264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Benjamin L. Stilwell" <just.bstil@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:45:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] inspect: optional winding-aware self-proximity for
 multi-wrap band surfaces

On a band that winds several times, every cell has a neighbor on the adjacent turn of the same sheet
a nearly constant grid offset away, so the self_proximity cue (grid-distant, 3D-close pairs) fires on the
whole surface. With winding_aware=True (CLI: inspect --winding-aware) pairs are grouped by grid offset in
log-scaled bins and a group holding at least winding_min_frac (default 0.5%) pairs per valid point is treated
as winding clearance and dropped. Local sheet switches and mirrored folds have varying offsets and are kept.
Default behavior is unchanged. Adds a test with a two-wrap band and a fold.
---
