From 4a6ff3c809b34357b2b77b986f6fa2d41ae3262a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Benjamin L. Stilwell" <just.bstil@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:21:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] winding-aware self-proximity: scale the pair-density
 requirement by the sampling stride

On grids above 400,000 valid cells inspect_patch subsamples every stride-th point, which divides the pair density
per sampled point by stride, so the fixed winding_min_frac could never be reached on large bands. The requirement
is now divided by the stride (unchanged when stride is 1). Found by validating on 24 multi-wrap PHercParis4 bands:
mean self-proximity flags 2.10 -> 0.14 per 1,000 cells.
---
 src/tifxyz_repair/deep.py | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/tifxyz_repair/deep.py b/src/tifxyz_repair/deep.py
